## Introduction
<!-- To-do (MUST HAVE): Provide a brief description of the project  -->
> **⚠️ Note** Updated after the publication of the research article

This repository contains an exemplary tool to estimate the tool condition for vibration-assisted drilling of multi-material stacks. The tools include:

1. **Feature extraction incl. Segmentation**: Timeseries data is segmented into the drilling phases (pre-drilling, entry into first material layer, drilling the first material layer, material interface, drilling the second layer, exit, post-drilling), and time- and frequency-domain-features are extracted.  
2. **Feature importance analysis**: Validation to estimate the importance of per-phase features vs. features computed for the overall signal and the importance for time- vs. frequency-domain-features.
3. **Transferability analysis**: 8 tools were used within this study. Four of them were drilled with a Keba LeviSpin spindle, four with a Keba LeviSpin HP spindle. Further, 5 tools were used for CFRP / C45 material stack, 3 were used to drill CFRP / 42CrMo4 stacks. These different data origins are used to study the transferability of the approach.


